<title>USA: DC arena costs inch up, but project on course-GAO.</title>
<headline>DC arena costs inch up, but project on course-GAO.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pre-construction costs for a planned $175 million downtown sports arena in the financially struggling District of Columbia are inching up, the General Accounting Office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But the district, which pledged to pay the costs largely through issuance of revenue bonds, has sufficient funds to pay the bills, GAO concluded in a 14-page report entitled &quot;Status of Sports Arena.&quot;</p>
</text>
